---
description: Never launch emulators, simulators, or app builds/runs from the agent terminal; the user runs the app on their own device
alwaysApply: true
---

# No emulators or app launches from the agent

- Never start an Android emulator or iOS simulator, in any form: `emulator`, `avdmanager`, Android Studio AVDs, `xcrun simctl`, or `npx expo run:android` / `run:ios` / `expo start --android` / `--ios` / `--web`.
- Never build or install the app on a device or emulator from the agent terminal (`gradlew assemble*`, `adb install`, `eas build`, `expo prebuild`).
- Do not start Metro or any dev server for the mobile app (`npx expo start`). The user starts it and runs the app on their physical device from their own terminal.
- `adb` may be used only for read-only diagnosis when the user asks (for example `adb devices`). Never use it to install, launch, or control the app.
- When a change needs the app to be run, say so and give the user the exact command to run themselves.
- Keep editing code and docs as normal; this rule only covers running the app and emulators.
